      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for actually taking this seriously. i've been feeling so gaslit by everyone telling me \"it's just stress.\" \n\nthe professional gear sounds expensive and i'm honestly scared that if i go to an official engineer, they'll just report it back to the company or tell me i'm crazy. i need to do some preliminary testing on my own first so i have hard data. \n\nif i wanted to build a DIY setup to try and isolate these sub-audible waves—maybe something to help shield my workspace or a way to create a counter-frequency to neutralize the signal—what kind of materials or wave principles should i be looking into? like, is there a way to create a \"null zone\" around my desk so i can actually work without this interference?",
